+# Unity Catalog compatibility e2e suite
+
+End-to-end tests for this fork's Unity Catalog-compatible API mounted at
+`/api/2.1/unity-catalog` (volumes, functions, registered models + versions,
+temporary credentials, read-mapped catalogs/schemas). Wire contract:
+`scratchpad/uc-api-contract.md`; semantics: `scratchpad/design-uc-objects.md`.
+
+## How to run
+
+```bash
+# full suite (default MODE=allowall)
+bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh
+
+# only the endpoints that already exist server-side (catalogs/schemas)
+bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh -m smoke
+
+# openfga stack verification (see "Modes" below)
+MODE=openfga bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh
+
+# reuse a previously built binary / leave the stack running for debugging
+SKIP_BUILD=1 KEEP_RUNNING=1 bash tests/uc-compat/run.sh -m smoke
+```
+
+`run.sh` builds `target/debug/lakekeeper` on the host, starts
+postgres/openfga/minio via `docker-compose.yaml`, runs `lakekeeper migrate`,
+starts `lakekeeper serve` on the host network, waits for `/health`, runs
+pytest, and tears everything down (server + `docker compose down -v`).
+
+Python dependencies (pinned in the e2e venv; `UC_TEST_PYTHON` to override):
+`unitycatalog-client==0.4.1`, `unitycatalog-ai==0.4.0`,
+`unitycatalog-langchain`, `unitycatalog-openai`, `boto3`, `duckdb`,
+`pyarrow`, `httpx`, `pytest`.
+
+## Modes
+
+| MODE | authn | authz | what runs |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `allowall` (default) | disabled (anonymous) | `LAKEKEEPER__AUTHZ_BACKEND=allowall` | everything: anonymous bootstrap works, full UC data-plane suite |
+| `openfga` | disabled (anonymous) | `LAKEKEEPER__AUTHZ_BACKEND=openfga` + gRPC to compose OpenFGA on `localhost:8081` | `test_authz.py` only |
+
+**Why MODE=openfga is limited:** the OpenFGA authorizer rejects anonymous
+bootstrap (`crates/authz-openfga/src/authorizer.rs`: "Anonymous users cannot
+bootstrap the catalog") and the fork has no dev/test authenticator — real
+authentication needs an OIDC IdP or Kubernetes tokens. MODE=openfga still
+proves: `lakekeeper migrate` creates the OpenFGA store and writes the fork's
+authorization model (incl. new volume/function/model FGA types once v4.8
+lands), the server serves with `authz-backend=openfga`, and anonymous
+bootstrap is properly rejected. Supplying `UC_TEST_TOKEN` (external IdP)
+additionally unlocks creator-owner-relation checks. TODO placeholder: add a
+keycloak service (realm-import pattern in `tests/docker-compose.yaml`) to run
+the full matrix hermetically.
+
+## Environment matrix
+
+| variable | default | meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `UC_TEST_BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:8181` | Lakekeeper base URL |
+| `UC_TEST_MODE` | `allowall` | `allowall` \| `openfga` (set by run.sh from `MODE`) |
+| `UC_TEST_TOKEN` | unset | optional bearer token (external IdP) |
+| `UC_TEST_S3_ENDPOINT` | `http://localhost:9000` | MinIO S3+STS endpoint |
+| `UC_TEST_S3_BUCKET` | `uc-e2e` | test bucket (created by `minio-init`) |
+| `UC_TEST_S3_KEY_PREFIX` | `warehouse` | warehouse key prefix in the bucket |
+| `UC_TEST_S3_ACCESS_KEY` / `UC_TEST_S3_SECRET_KEY` | `lakekeeper` / `lakekeeper-secret` | non-root MinIO user used as warehouse storage credential |
+| `UC_TEST_WAREHOUSE` | `uc_e2e` | warehouse name == UC catalog name |
+
+## Vended credentials against MinIO
+
+The `uc_e2e` warehouse is created with an S3 storage profile:
+`endpoint`/`sts-endpoint` → MinIO, `path-style-access: true`,
+`flavor: s3-compat`, `sts-enabled: true`, no `sts-role-arn` (per
+`docs/docs/storage.md`, S3-compatible stores need neither role ARN nor trust
+setup — Lakekeeper calls MinIO's AssumeRole with the configured access key).
+The credential is a dedicated non-root `lakekeeper` user (created by the
+`minio-init` container with the `readwrite` policy) because MinIO applies
+STS *session policies* — which give READ_VOLUME/WRITE_VOLUME creds their
+downscoped semantics — as an intersection with an IAM user's policy.
+
+## What each file proves
+
+| file | coverage |
+|---|---|
+| `test_catalogs_schemas.py` (`-m smoke`) | catalog=warehouse read mapping; catalogs read-only (400); schema CRUD = top-level namespaces; pagination envelope; 404/409 error mapping |
+| `test_volumes.py` | volume CRUD (MANAGED location generation, EXTERNAL location validation), pagination, PATCH comment / rename rejected, 409 conflict, delete→`{}`→404; `temporary-volume-credentials` shape; **engines**: boto3 put/get with vended creds, read-only downscoping (best-effort), DuckDB httpfs reads volume parquet with vended keys |
+| `test_functions.py` | **unitycatalog-ai** `create_python_function` → get/list → local `execute_function`; **LangChain** `UCFunctionToolkit` tool direct invocation (no LLM); **OpenAI** toolkit JSON-schema generation (no API call); raw-SDK round-trip fidelity (`routine_definition`, `input_params` positions), no PATCH endpoint, 404 mapping |
+| `test_models.py` | registered-model CRUD; **MLflow-style flow**: version PENDING → READ_WRITE creds → boto3 artifact upload → finalize READY → READ_WRITE rejected → READ creds download; version auto-increment; delete-with-versions guard |
+| `test_authz.py` (`-m authz`, MODE=openfga) | openfga backend live, FGA store/model migration, anonymous-bootstrap rejection; owner-relation checks behind `UC_TEST_TOKEN` |
+
+## Notes / known constraints
+
+* unitycatalog-client 0.4.1 is async (aiohttp ≥3.10 requires constructing the
+  client inside a running loop); `conftest.UcSdk` runs a dedicated
+  background event loop. unitycatalog-ai's sync facade is bridged via
+  `uc_ai` (nest_asyncio inside `run_until_complete`) — see conftest docstring.
+* The DuckDB test needs the `httpfs` extension; it skips cleanly if the
+  extension cannot be downloaded in an offline environment.
+* Volumes/functions/models endpoints are being implemented concurrently
+  (design phases B-D); until they land only `-m smoke` passes.
